Chapter: RocMatchIntoArithmetic
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_match_tests.zig, "match-dt:
 match result flows into surrounding arithmetic":

     f : Try(I64, {}) -> I64
     f = |v| 1 + (match v { Ok(n) => n * 2, Err({}) => -10 }) * 10
     main = (f(Ok(3)), f(Err({})))                        (61, -99)

 The `when` is an operand, parenthesised inside `1 + (...) * 10`. Roc's
 empty-record error payload is an Integer here, never read.

Section: Types

  Res (a) (e) =
   | Ok (a)
   | Err (e)

Section: Functions

  f : Res Integer Integer -> Integer
  f (v) =
   1 + (when v
    is Ok (n) -> n * 2
    is Err (ignored) -> 0 - 10) * 10

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (f (Ok 3)))
   print-line-uni (show (f (Err 0)))
  end
